zip-slip:-1 4
  ok.txt
  ../evil.txt
  /tmp/rapidr-abs.txt
  sub/../../up.txt
  ExtractAll=0
  "../evil.txt" goes up a folder (..): not extracted (it would be written outside the folder); nothing was extracted
  written:000
  ok.txt:zip-slip test
link:-1 3
  ok.txt
  escape
  escape/rapidr-through-link.txt
  [] "escape" is a link: links aren't extracted (one could point outside the folder)
bomb:-1 zeros.bin says 31457280 bytes in -1
  0 "zeros.bin" unpacks to more than MaxRatio (1000) times its packed size: not unpacked — a zip bomb, or set MaxRatio higher
  0 "zeros.bin" unpacks to more than MaxSize (1000000 bytes): not unpacked — a zip bomb, or set MaxSize higher
  MaxSize 0 means the default:-1
encrypted zip:-1 readme.txt -1
  [] "readme.txt" is encrypted: RArchive doesn't open password-protected entries
encrypted 7z:0 the 7z archive is encrypted: RArchive doesn't open password-protected archives
rar:rar 0
  RAR files can't be opened: the format isn't open. Ask for a .zip or .7z.
cut:0 not a zip, or a damaged one (its list of files can't be found)
changed:-1 3 [-1] -1
not an archive:0 not an archive RapidR knows (zip, 7z, tar, tar.gz, gz, xz, zst)
no file:0 can't read no-such-archive.zip: no such file, or it can't be read
